From bc30698dfb495eef5eded7bcd4cea6fb484d0e39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:12:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/57] hw/avr: AVR8X SoC and the avr64ea48-cnano machine

avr8x-soc builds an AVRxt device from its generated descriptor: flash in
the program space and, through NVMCTRL.CTRLB.FLMAP, in a 32 KB data-space
window; SRAM; EEPROM (also at avr-gcc's .eeprom load address 0x810000);
CCP; one mchp-regblock per I/O instance, connected to the CPU's interrupt
inputs by vector number; everything without a model logs its accesses.

Dedicated models (DS40002324, AVR64EA48):
- avr8x-port: PORTA-F and VPORTA-F in one device: DIR/OUT with
  SET/CLR/TGL, IN (write 1 toggles OUT), PINnCTRL (ISC, PULLUPEN, INVEN)
  and the PINCONFIG multi-pin update, INTFLAGS, pads, external drivers,
  peripheral overrides and the per-pad duty statistics the web view
  reads ("p<x>-levels", "p<x>-stats").
- avr8x-usart: asynchronous USART, TX buffer and shift register (DREIF,
  TXCIF), 2-character RX FIFO, RXC/DRE/TXC interrupts, optional pacing
  at the baud rate from CLK_PER.
- avr8x-clkctrl: CLK_PER from CLKSEL and the prescaler (OSCHF 20 MHz / 6
  at reset), oscillator status.
- avr8x-cpuint: CPUINT registers on the CPU's interrupt state.
- avr8x-nvmctrl: FLMAP; NVM commands are logged.
- avr8x-nvmbytes: SIGROW (signature), SYSCFG (REVID), USERROW, FUSE, LOCK.

avr64ea48-cnano: the AVR64EA48 Curiosity Nano (EV66E56A): LED0 on PB3
(active low), SW0 on PB2 ("sw0-pressed"), the virtual COM port on USART1
(serial 0), USART2 on serial 1; firmware from -kernel or -bios.
firmware/avr-hello prints byte for byte what the kit printed
(golden/avr64ea48-b1/hello-vcom.bin) with an empty model backlog.
qtest: identity, memory map and FLMAP, PORT/VPORT/LED0/SW0, USART flags,
CPUINT.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
